comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T17:04:45.941Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: inspected all-status pm search results plus full live metadata/comments/history for closed pm-yffj and pm-3ljt19. Those items delivered diagnostic payloads and earlier command-boundary propagation, but GH-882 reproduces a current 2026.8.3 classifier/order/recovery regression where the payload exists and the headline/remediation remain false. Related GH-772/pm-4vwcvq concerns rejected registration rather than import-time activation failure. Canonical GitHub report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/882"
  "2026-08-03T18:40:15.748Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: unresolved-command recovery now correlates the attempted command with statically declared extension command paths before generic typo guidance. Matching activation failures lead human output and populate extension_command_failure in JSON; dependency-install remediation appears only when the failure matches the requested path. End-to-end coverage installs a broken clone-like extension and asserts the false Unknown command diagnosis no longer leads."
  "2026-08-03T19:02:41.643Z","harness:codex","Hosted contract follow-up: the new extension_command_activation_failed code is now included in the generated public error-code catalog and the full contract snapshot. The exact contracts:check pipeline passes after generating the catalog before refreshing the snapshot."
  "2026-08-03T19:30:44.643Z","harness:codex","Exact-head PR evidence (PR #884, c361624e2): every hosted required check passes, including static/typecheck/coverage/smokes/compat, Ubuntu/macOS/Windows runtime smoke, benchmarks, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, DeepScan, CodeFactor, Codecov, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, and Docs/Skills. The complete sandboxed local suite passes 428 files / 6,792 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; lint, zero-clone analysis, 100% docstring gates, contracts, and focused review regressions pass. All 12 CodeRabbit threads were individually replied to and reacted to; nine actionable findings were fixed in c361624e2 and all threads are resolved. The requested exact-head CodeRabbit rerun was included-review-rate-limited and the authenticated Greptile gate returned free_reviews_limit_reached; these are reviewer limitations, not clean-review claims."
  "2026-08-03T19:40:15.976Z","harness:codex","Merge and operational evidence: PR #884 merged to main as 657f8fa56a1e56c918095a58600c49188206e180; local main equals origin/main and the worktree is clean. No open PRs remain; GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning each report zero open alerts; pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities. Telemetry flush at 2026-08-03T19:36:53.267Z successfully drained four queued events, while subsequent status commands generated fresh self-observability rows. Live Sentry 14-day data shows no new issue attributable to this tranche; older unresolved PM-CLI-2S and PM-CLI-2Q remain independently tracked by open pm-4odf0c and pm-qyg51h. The sole immutable same-day tag/package remains v2026.8.3 / @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.3; the scheduled Auto Release already proved same-day no-op behavior after that release, so this post-tag merge is intentionally eligible for the next UTC daily release rather than creating or moving a duplicate same-day version."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:16.200Z","harness:codex","Privacy and relevance boundary: recovery exposes the extension identity and bounded sanitized failure context but does not offer dependency repair for unrelated activation failures or leak arbitrary module paths."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:16.582Z","harness:codex","Collecting activation failures is insufficient if the command-boundary classifier ignores contribution ownership. Recovery must join attempted command path, static contribution inventory, and activation result before rendering generic suggestions."
